          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উপন্যাস (upônyās) is Sanskrit upanyāsa, 'a putting down, a placing near' (Monier-Williams); the sense 'a novel' is the modern Bengali one."
            }
          ]
        },
